# Deliberately no `migration:` block. Current Flutter writes one whose
# base_revision asserts that android/, ios/ and web/ already sit at that
# revision's template baseline. They do not - those directories are still
# Flutter 2.x-era and hand-customised, and the actual template migration has
# not been run. Recording a new baseline here would tell future `flutter
# upgrade`/`flutter create .` runs that nothing needs migrating and quietly
# hide the real template diff. Add the block by running the template migration
# for real, not by editing this file.
